#: src/ubuntu_start.py:240
msgid "Use the Terminal"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:240 src/ubuntu_start.py:2602
msgid "Open Terminal"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:241
msgid "What the prompt means"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:241
msgid ""
"The prompt is the text before the cursor. It shows that the terminal is "
"ready for a command. Type after it; do not type the prompt itself."
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:242
msgid "Run a command"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:242
msgid ""
"Type a command and press Enter to run it. For example, pwd shows the current "
"folder and ls lists its files. These commands only show information."
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:243
msgid "Read the result"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:243
msgid ""
"Commands may print information or an error message. Read the last lines "
"first. If a command finishes without an error, it may return to the prompt "
"without printing anything."
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:244
msgid "Copy and paste safely"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:244
msgid ""
"Copy text with Ctrl+Shift+C and paste with Ctrl+Shift+V. Before pasting a "
"command, read all of it: some terminals can run multiple pasted lines, and "
"commands may change or delete files."
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:245
msgid "Move between folders"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:245
msgid ""
"Use cd Documents to enter a folder and cd .. to go up one level. Use pwd to "
"check where you are."
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:246
msgid "Use Tab and command history"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:246
msgid ""
"Press Tab to complete a file or folder name when it is unique. Press the Up "
"Arrow to find a command you used earlier; check it before pressing Enter."
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:247
msgid "Type paths with spaces"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:247
msgid ""
"Put quotation marks around a folder or file name that contains spaces, for "
"example: cd \"My Documents\". You can also type the first letters and press "
"Tab to complete the name."
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:248
msgid "Ask a command for help"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:248
msgid ""
"Try a command followed by --help, such as ls --help. For more detail, use "
"man followed by the command name; press q to leave the manual."
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:249
msgid "Understand sudo"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:249
msgid ""
"sudo runs a command with administrator privileges. Use it only when you "
"understand and trust the command. Your password is not shown while you type "
"it."
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:250
msgid "Enter a password at a prompt"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:250
msgid ""
"When sudo or another trusted tool asks for your password, typing may show no "
"letters or dots. Type it only if you expected the prompt and trust the "
"command, then press Enter. Press Ctrl+C if the prompt is unexpected; never "
"share your password."
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:251
msgid "Wait for a command to finish"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:251
msgid ""
"While a command is working, the prompt may not appear. Wait for it to return "
"before typing another command. Some commands take time. Ctrl+C asks a "
"command to stop but cannot undo changes already made; do not close the "
"terminal during system updates or file operations."
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:252
msgid "Stop a running command"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:252
msgid ""
"Ctrl+C asks the current command to stop. It does not undo changes the "
"command has already made."
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:253
msgid "Keep commands from trusted sources"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:253
msgid ""
"Do not paste commands you do not understand, especially commands using sudo, "
"rm, disk tools or scripts downloaded from the internet."
msgstr ""

